## 6. RFC 7807 ERROR FORMAT (5 Required Properties)

```json
{
  "type": "/errors/not-found",
  "title": "Not Found",
  "status": 404,
  "detail": "Customer with ID 'xyz' not found",
  "instance": "/customers/xyz"
}
```

| Property | Required | Most Forgotten |
|----------|----------|----------------|
| `type` | ✅ | |
| `title` | ✅ | |
| `status` | ✅ | |
| `detail` | ✅ | |
| `instance` | ✅ | **YES - Often missed!** |

---

## 7. CRITICAL PITFALLS

| # | Pitfall | ❌ Wrong | ✅ Correct |
|---|---------|---------|-----------|
| 1 | Inline examples | Embedded in RAML | `!include examples/...` |
| 2 | Security refs | `SecuritySchemes.X` | `!include fragments/security-schemes/...` |
| 3 | Missing RFC 7807 | Forgetting `instance` | All 5 properties |
| 4 | Over-engineering | 12 endpoints | Confirm needs first |
| 5 | DataType deps | Extending library types | Self-contained fragments |
| 6 | Large RAML | Inline everything | Externalize to fragments |
| 7 | Missing headers | No fragment header | `#%RAML 1.0 DataType` etc. |
| 8 | Repeated error blocks | 30 lines × 5 endpoints | Consolidate into error-responses trait |
| 9 | Trait path resolution | `!include examples/...` in trait | `!include ../examples/...` from trait location |

