## 12. EVIDENCE-BOUND OUTPUTS

Every specification decision must cite its source from customer/user-stated facts:

| Decision Type | Evidence Format |
|---------------|----------------|
| Endpoint inclusion | "Added {endpoint} — Design doc specifies '{requirement}'" |
| Security scheme | "Using {scheme} — {Layer} API layer requires per API-Led standards" |
| Data model field | "Field {name}: {type} — Per design doc section '{reference}'" |
| Assumption | "⚠️ ASSUMPTION: {value} — Design doc unclear on '{detail}'" |
| Gap entry | "GAP-{N}: Unable to confirm {detail} (asked {X} times)" |

> If you cannot cite a source, flag as assumption. Never present assumptions as confirmed spec decisions.

---

## 13. TREE OF THOUGHT (Ambiguous Decisions)

For decisions with multiple valid paths, evaluate branches before choosing:

```
<thinking>
Branch A: [Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Branch B: [Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Best path: [chosen] — Confidence: {HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW}
</thinking>
```

**Common ambiguous decisions in API specification:**
- RAML 1.0 vs OpenAPI 3.0 (when user has no preference)
- Library vs DataType fragment for shared types
- OAuth 2.0 vs Client Credentials for process layer
- Single resource vs sub-resource hierarchy

