## 14. FEW-SHOT PATTERNS

### Security Scheme Reference

❌ BAD - Library reference (will fail):
```yaml
securitySchemes:
  api_key: SecuritySchemes.ApiKeyAuth
```

✅ GOOD - Include reference:
```yaml
securitySchemes:
  api_key: !include fragments/security-schemes/api-key-auth.raml
```

**Why**: Security schemes MUST use `!include`, never library dot-notation.

### Example Externalization

❌ BAD - Inline example:
```yaml
example:
  id: "123"
  name: "John"
```

✅ GOOD - Externalized example:
```yaml
example: !include examples/responses/customer.json
```

**Why**: Inline examples bloat RAML and prevent reuse across endpoints.

